Port of rexglue-sdk#530: Memory::Initialize creates the guest address-space mapping with a new
CreateFileMappingHandle overload that shm_unlinks the POSIX name once the descriptor is open, so a crashed or
SIGKILLed run no longer leaves a ~4.8 GB xenia_memory_* object in /dev/shm. The four-argument overload keeps the
named mapping and delegates with false; the Windows overload ignores the flag. Includes the upstream unit tests.

